===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ca|pro|}}, from {{inh|ca|VL.||*facla}}, contracted form of {{inh|ca|la|facula||little torch}}, diminutive of {{m|la|fax}}. Compare the borrowed doublet {{doublet|ca|fàcula|notext=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# constructions of inflammable materials, based in figures that are caricatures (the [[ninot|ninots]]) that are installed in certain [[Valencian]] municipalities and are burned to ashes the day of Saint Joseph.
# the holidays around these constructions.
# the associations or organizations around these constructions.
# [[fire]], [[bonfire]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|ca|fallir}}, or alternatively a {{inh|ca|VL.||falla}} or {{m|la||*falia}}, from {{inh|ca|pro|fallō}}.

====Noun====
